{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nFound while surveying the credential-in-argv class for antiviral-agrarian-amurminnow (2026-11-22 PST). Operator-workstation tooling and contributor guidance still put Gerrit credentials on a process command line, where any local user or process monitor can read them while the process runs:\n- `infra/gerrit/service-user.sh` (the bot-token rotation tool): `ssh ... gerrit create-account/set-account --http-password \"$TOKEN\"` (lines 41-55; the new token is in the local ssh argv), `aws ssm put-parameter --value \"$TOKEN\"` (line 66), and `awk -v tok=\"$TOKEN\"` (line 83).\n- `infra/gerrit/smoke-check.sh`, `reviewbot-e2e.sh`, `feature-branch-e2e.sh`, `feature-branch-e2e-scenarios.sh` and `feature-branch-inventory.sh`: `curl -u \"user:$PW\"`, and `git clone`/`git push` or `curl` with `https://user:$PW@host` URLs.\n- `.github/workflows/external-integration.yml:783,787`: the Jira cleanup's `curl -u \"${JIRA_USER}:${JIRA_API_TOKEN}\"`.\n- `AGENTS.md:90` (the recommended Gerrit REST snippet) and `CONTRIBUTING.md:268-270` teach `curl --user \"$user:$password\"` / `curl -u \"$USER:$PASS\"`.\n\nThese run on operator hosts, not the review-bot box, so they were kept out of the box-side fix (antiviral-agrarian-amurminnow), which adds a static guard over `src/rebar`; this ticket extends that guard to the files above. service-user.sh is the tool the operator would use to rotate the review-bot token, so fixing it before that rotation keeps the new token out of argv.\n\n## Approach\nRoot cause: each script builds the credential into a command-line argument (`curl -u user:pw`, `https://user:pw@host`, `ssh ... --http-password <tok>`, `aws ... --value <tok>`, `awk -v tok=<tok>`); argv is readable by every local user via `ps` and `/proc/<pid>/cmdline` while the process runs. Fix: hand each credential over a non-argv channel. `printf` is a shell builtin, so `printf ... | cmd` moves it through a pipe without a process carrying it.\n\n1. New sourced `infra/gerrit/lib-credentials.sh`:\n   - `curl_auth <user> <pw> <curl args>`: escapes `\\` and `\"`, then `printf 'user = \"%s:%s\"\\n' | curl -K - \"$@\"`. Measured 2026-11-23: a local HTTP server received the expected Basic header, including for a password with `\"` and `\\`.\n   - `git_auth <base-url> <user> <pw> <git args>`: runs git with git's own `GIT_CONFIG_COUNT`/`KEY_<n>`/`VALUE_<n>` env (appended after inherited entries) carrying `credential.helper=` (empty, so the operator's keychain helper is not asked, stored to or erased) and `http.<base-url>/.extraHeader = Authorization: Basic ...`, plus `GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT=0`. Same mechanism as the box fix 053604a2618; git-defined variables only, no new rebar env var, config key or flag.\n2. `infra/gerrit/service-user.sh`: `create-account` drops `--http-password`; for new and existing accounts it deletes the `default` token (as today) and runs `gerrit set-account <bot> --generate-http-password`, which Gerrit 3.14.1 (deployed image, `infra/compose/Dockerfile.gerrit:5`) answers on stdout with `New password: <pw>`. The script captures it without echoing, strips the prefix and CR, and exits 1 without printing unless the value is non-empty and only `[A-Za-z0-9+/=._~-]`. Every consumer of `/rebar/prod/gerrit-bot-token` uses it in a header or the 0600 env file, so this charset needs no URL encoding. SSM: `printf '%s' \"$TOKEN\" | aws ssm put-parameter ... --value file:///dev/stdin` (measured with AWS CLI 2.39.7 via a read-only `get-parameter --name file:///dev/stdin`: the request carried the stdin value). The template render becomes a bash `while read` loop with `${line//__BOT_TOKEN__/$TOKEN}` (no process; the charset check excludes `&` and `\\`).\n3. `smoke-check.sh`, `reviewbot-e2e.sh`, `feature-branch-e2e.sh`, `feature-branch-e2e-scenarios.sh`, `feature-branch-inventory.sh` source the helper: every `curl -u` becomes `curl_auth`; the 2 URL-userinfo git calls become `git_auth` with a userinfo-free URL; the reviewbot-e2e hook download uses `curl_auth`.\n4. `.github/workflows/external-integration.yml` Jira cleanup: `printf 'user = ...' | curl -K -`.\n5. Docs: `AGENTS.md` and `CONTRIBUTING.md` REST examples and `infra/runbooks/gerrit-auth-hardening.md:120` use `printf 'user = ...' | curl --config -`. Same class, also fixed: `infra/runbooks/review-bot-ops.md:152` (`X-Rebar-Token` via `-K -` `header =`), `infra/runbooks/g2p-ci-credentials.md:97` and `docs/gerrit-aws-setup.md:443` (`--value file://<keyfile>`), `infra/runbooks/sso-auth-host.md:131` (generated secret piped to `file:///dev/stdin`).\n6. Out of scope: `docs/mcp-client-setup.md` (MCP client PAT in `mcp add --header`; fix depends on vendor `${VAR}` expansion) is filed as limitless-defaceable-beaver and named in one guard exclusion citing it. IMDSv2 `X-aws-ec2-metadata-token` headers are excluded by pattern (short-lived instance-local session tokens).\n\n## Scope\n- `infra/gerrit/`: `lib-credentials.sh` (new), `service-user.sh`, `smoke-check.sh`, `reviewbot-e2e.sh`, `feature-branch-e2e.sh`, `feature-branch-e2e-scenarios.sh`, `feature-branch-inventory.sh`\n- `.github/workflows/external-integration.yml`, `AGENTS.md`, `CONTRIBUTING.md`, `docs/gerrit-aws-setup.md`, `infra/runbooks/{gerrit-auth-hardening,review-bot-ops,g2p-ci-credentials,sso-auth-host}.md`\n- Tests: `tests/unit/test_review_bot_git_credential_argv.py` (extend guard), `tests/scripts/test_operator_credential_argv.py` (new), `tests/scripts/test_feature_branch_inventory.py` (curl stub drains `-K -` stdin)\n- No `src/rebar` change; no rotation; `service-user.sh` is not run.\n\n## Testing\n- Static guard: scans `infra/**/*.{sh,md}`, `scripts/**/*.sh`, `.github/workflows/*`, `docs/**/*.md`, `AGENTS.md`, `CONTRIBUTING.md` for `-u`/`--user` with a `$`/`<` password, URL userinfo with a `$`/`<` password, `--http-password`, `--value \"$(cat|openssl...\"`/`\"$<secret var>\"`, `awk -v x=\"$<secret var>\"`, and an auth/token header from a variable. Parametrized self-tests: each pattern flags its target shape and passes the fixed and unrelated shapes. On the pre-fix tree it reports 28 hits; after, none.\n- `service-user.sh` end to end against argv-recording `ssh`/`aws`/`git` stubs (create and rotate paths, template copy with `__BOT_TOKEN__`): the token is in no argv and no output; aws gets it exactly on stdin; the render contains it. Malformed generator output (empty, extra text, `&`, `\\`) exits non-zero, never calls aws, never prints it.\n- Helpers: no secret in argv; curl stdin config round-trips `\"` and `\\` (stub, and real curl against a local server); git env order with an inherited entry; malformed inherited count; real `git config --get-urlmatch` resolves the header for Gerrit and not for github.com.\n- Existing guidance/workflow/inventory tests keep passing; shell tests use `requires_posix_shell`; `make verify` before push.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `infra/gerrit/service-user.sh` passes the new token to `aws ssm put-parameter` and to the webhooks template render without it appearing in any argv (for example `--value file://` from a pipe, and `ENVIRON` in awk), and sets the Gerrit HTTP password without it appearing in the local ssh argv (for example server-side generation, or the REST endpoint with the body on stdin).\n- [ ] The Gerrit REST examples in `AGENTS.md` and `CONTRIBUTING.md` pass the credential through `curl -K` from a pipe (or another channel that is not argv), not `-u`/`--user`.\n- [ ] The static guard test added by antiviral-agrarian-amurminnow covers these files and passes."}},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1795428446039879001,"uuid":"379da31f-fb76-404c-8a97-963e2fe81d3f"}